                        <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_247">Hereford, Herefordshire,
                                Cathedral church of St Ethelbert</orgName><p>The index card for the
                                Mordiford parish church provenance (see below) also notes the
                                following: <q>The manuscript appears to have been in use at the
                                    cathedral in s. xiii ex to judge from the obits.</q> However, no
                                dedicated index card for the Hereford provenance was found during
                                MLGB data reconciliation work in 2026. The Hereford provenance also
                                appears to have been accidentally omitted from MLGB2 and the
                                Supplement. Compare <bibl> Michael Gullick, Michael, R. A. B.
                                    Mynors, and Rodney M. Thomson, <title>Catalogue of the
                                        Manuscripts of Hereford Cathedral Library</title>
                                    (Cambridge, 1993), p. 125</bibl>: "Made for Hereford Cathedral,
                                as the obits in art.3 show. Among the obits in the original hand,
                                Canon Richard de Monte Garnerii was still alive in 1262, while
                                Bishop Aquablanca, whose name is an early addition, died in 1268. At
                                the parish church of Mordiford by s. xv ex." </p></provenance>
                        <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_887">Mordiford, Herefordshire.
                                Parish church</orgName>
                            <p><q>Dedicacio ecclesie parrochialis de mordiford</q> at June 4 (fol.
                                185v). Obits of the Crikelot family.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners">Purchased in 1834 from Mr
                                <persName>William Hawes</persName> who had bought it from a stall in
                            Drury Lane.</provenance>
